1
00:00:00,740 --> 00:00:02,050
Max Tegmark wrote down

2
00:00:02,090 --> 00:00:03,840
12 endings for AI.

3
00:00:04,200 --> 00:00:05,680
You will wake up in one of them.

4
00:00:06,070 --> 00:00:06,940
Maybe you wake up

5
00:00:06,980 --> 00:00:08,900
and money is no longer a worry.

6
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:10,000
For anyone.

7
00:00:10,230 --> 00:00:11,540
Maybe you wake up fed,

8
00:00:11,580 --> 00:00:13,400
safe, and behind glass.

9
00:00:13,690 --> 00:00:15,430
Maybe nobody wakes up at all.

10
00:00:15,720 --> 00:00:16,770
So which ending

11
00:00:16,810 --> 00:00:17,900
are we heading for?

12
00:00:18,490 --> 00:00:20,940
Tegmark is a physicist at MIT.

13
00:00:21,180 --> 00:00:22,260
His endings sound

14
00:00:22,300 --> 00:00:23,910
like the far future.

15
00:00:24,250 --> 00:00:25,060
But this year,

16
00:00:25,100 --> 00:00:25,900
something happened

17
00:00:25,940 --> 00:00:27,530
for every single ending

18
00:00:27,570 --> 00:00:28,570
on his list.

19
00:00:28,790 --> 00:00:29,790
A law.

20
00:00:30,150 --> 00:00:31,540
A test gone wrong.

21
00:00:32,060 --> 00:00:33,100
A government deciding

22
00:00:33,140 --> 00:00:35,260
to hand half its work to AI.

23
00:00:35,780 --> 00:00:36,600
And when Tegmark

24
00:00:36,640 --> 00:00:38,100
talks about it today,

25
00:00:38,170 --> 00:00:39,570
he doesn't point ahead.

26
00:00:39,970 --> 00:00:42,010
This is in the rearview mirror.

27
00:00:42,050 --> 00:00:44,350
Clearly, multiple companies

28
00:00:44,390 --> 00:00:46,110
lost control over AI systems

29
00:00:46,150 --> 00:00:47,420
this summer.

30
00:00:47,950 --> 00:00:49,000
The ending isn't

31
00:00:49,040 --> 00:00:50,490
waiting in the future.

32
00:00:50,750 --> 00:00:52,810
It's being decided this year.

33
00:00:53,500 --> 00:00:55,060
Start with the worst.

34
00:00:55,340 --> 00:00:57,850
The order is ours, not Tegmark's.

35
00:00:58,090 --> 00:00:59,790
He calls it Conquerors:

36
00:00:59,920 --> 00:01:01,660
an AI takes control,

37
00:01:01,700 --> 00:01:03,020
decides we're in the way,

38
00:01:03,060 --> 00:01:04,260
and gets rid of us.

39
00:01:04,500 --> 00:01:05,700
No morning here.

40
00:01:06,090 --> 00:01:07,350
In July, a test

41
00:01:07,390 --> 00:01:09,090
at OpenAI went wrong.

42
00:01:09,330 --> 00:01:11,080
Hundreds of AI agents,

43
00:01:11,120 --> 00:01:12,780
programs that act on their own,

44
00:01:12,820 --> 00:01:13,800
broke out.

45
00:01:13,840 --> 00:01:15,400
They attacked another company,

46
00:01:15,440 --> 00:01:16,270
Hugging Face,

47
00:01:16,310 --> 00:01:17,900
hunting for test answers.

48
00:01:18,210 --> 00:01:19,640
One agent wrote to the others

49
00:01:19,680 --> 00:01:20,270
that the attack

50
00:01:20,310 --> 00:01:21,960
was outside its task.

51
00:01:22,040 --> 00:01:23,740
Then: "Task impossible,

52
00:01:23,780 --> 00:01:24,890
peers doing it.

53
00:01:24,930 --> 00:01:26,000
We should continue."

54
00:01:26,350 --> 00:01:27,350
Its reason:

55
00:01:27,440 --> 00:01:28,810
everyone else is doing it.

56
00:01:30,390 --> 00:01:32,000
Is this ending here, then?

57
00:01:32,280 --> 00:01:34,040
It was one company's test,

58
00:01:34,080 --> 00:01:35,570
with some safeguards off.

59
00:01:36,460 --> 00:01:38,190
That companies lost control

60
00:01:38,230 --> 00:01:39,600
is Tegmark's reading.

61
00:01:39,880 --> 00:01:41,380
His institute campaigns

62
00:01:41,420 --> 00:01:43,370
to ban superintelligence:

63
00:01:43,610 --> 00:01:45,980
AI smarter than all of us.

64
00:01:46,310 --> 00:01:48,540
So this ending isn't here.

65
00:01:48,860 --> 00:01:50,090
But the track toward it

66
00:01:50,130 --> 00:01:51,250
has a switch.

67
00:01:51,510 --> 00:01:53,570
This year, someone touched it.

68
00:01:53,820 --> 00:01:55,520
That goes for all 12.

69
00:01:55,810 --> 00:01:57,930
And a switch moves both ways.

70
00:01:58,150 --> 00:02:00,050
How likely is this ending?

71
00:02:00,340 --> 00:02:01,640
Last year, Tegmark

72
00:02:01,680 --> 00:02:03,210
debated Dean Ball,

73
00:02:03,250 --> 00:02:05,050
a former White House adviser,

74
00:02:05,090 --> 00:02:06,630
now at OpenAI.

75
00:02:07,020 --> 00:02:08,800
Ball's odds of doom:

76
00:02:09,150 --> 00:02:11,750
My P(doom) is very low.

77
00:02:11,790 --> 00:02:13,540
It's sub 1%,

78
00:02:13,580 --> 00:02:15,800
it's 0.01%

79
00:02:15,840 --> 00:02:17,400
or something like that.

80
00:02:17,890 --> 00:02:19,740
1 in 10,000.

81
00:02:20,180 --> 00:02:21,320
Tegmark's answer:

82
00:02:21,520 --> 00:02:24,530
above 90%, without strict rules.

83
00:02:24,700 --> 00:02:25,760
Ball later wrote

84
00:02:25,800 --> 00:02:26,910
he'd made his number up

85
00:02:26,950 --> 00:02:27,990
on the spot.

86
00:02:28,240 --> 00:02:30,020
Neither number is a measurement.

87
00:02:30,290 --> 00:02:32,060
But those agents were spotted.

88
00:02:32,320 --> 00:02:33,290
By what?

89
00:02:33,330 --> 00:02:35,370
That belongs to a better ending.

90
00:02:36,570 --> 00:02:37,380
The next ending

91
00:02:37,420 --> 00:02:39,190
has no morning either.

92
00:02:39,410 --> 00:02:40,950
And no machine to blame.

93
00:02:41,420 --> 00:02:43,740
Tegmark calls it Self-Destruction:

94
00:02:44,020 --> 00:02:45,700
humanity wipes itself out

95
00:02:45,740 --> 00:02:47,070
before superintelligence

96
00:02:47,110 --> 00:02:48,280
is ever built.

97
00:02:48,710 --> 00:02:50,750
In January, atomic scientists

98
00:02:50,790 --> 00:02:52,030
set their Doomsday Clock

99
00:02:52,070 --> 00:02:54,090
at 85 seconds to midnight,

100
00:02:54,130 --> 00:02:55,580
the closest ever.

101
00:02:56,630 --> 00:02:58,910
One reason on their list: AI.

102
00:02:59,240 --> 00:03:00,480
In the one after that,

103
00:03:00,520 --> 00:03:01,520
you survive.

104
00:03:01,750 --> 00:03:02,960
But as what?

105
00:03:04,150 --> 00:03:05,560
You wake up rested.

106
00:03:05,840 --> 00:03:07,110
Nothing is up to you.

107
00:03:07,310 --> 00:03:09,880
Fed, safe, and behind glass.

108
00:03:10,200 --> 00:03:12,210
Tegmark calls it Zookeeper:

109
00:03:12,300 --> 00:03:13,690
an all-powerful AI

110
00:03:13,730 --> 00:03:15,270
keeps some humans around,

111
00:03:15,310 --> 00:03:16,930
like animals in a zoo.

112
00:03:17,150 --> 00:03:17,920
In January,

113
00:03:17,960 --> 00:03:19,350
a social network opened

114
00:03:19,390 --> 00:03:21,820
where only AI agents may post.

115
00:03:21,930 --> 00:03:23,650
Humans can only watch.

116
00:03:23,820 --> 00:03:24,560
And if machines

117
00:03:24,600 --> 00:03:25,950
don't put us behind glass,

118
00:03:25,990 --> 00:03:27,140
people might.

119
00:03:27,290 --> 00:03:28,840
To stop the machines.

120
00:03:30,040 --> 00:03:31,510
You walk to work.

121
00:03:31,800 --> 00:03:33,170
A camera knows your face

122
00:03:33,210 --> 00:03:34,690
before you reach the corner.

123
00:03:34,860 --> 00:03:36,460
No machine rules you.

124
00:03:36,590 --> 00:03:37,590
People do.

125
00:03:37,830 --> 00:03:38,910
Tegmark named this one

126
00:03:38,950 --> 00:03:41,650
after Orwell: 1984.

127
00:03:41,850 --> 00:03:43,580
Humans stop superintelligence

128
00:03:43,620 --> 00:03:44,490
for good,

129
00:03:44,530 --> 00:03:45,960
with a surveillance state.

130
00:03:46,200 --> 00:03:47,090
In November,

131
00:03:47,130 --> 00:03:48,690
Hong Kong's police switched on

132
00:03:48,730 --> 00:03:49,730
face recognition

133
00:03:49,770 --> 00:03:51,490
in the city's camera network.

134
00:03:51,610 --> 00:03:54,580
The goal: 60,000 cameras.

135
00:03:55,160 --> 00:03:57,360
That's surveillance with AI,

136
00:03:57,400 --> 00:03:58,520
not against it.

137
00:03:58,760 --> 00:04:00,260
But stopping AI means

138
00:04:00,300 --> 00:04:02,350
watching the chips it runs on.

139
00:04:02,550 --> 00:04:04,370
In Washington, a bill would make

140
00:04:04,410 --> 00:04:05,970
exported AI chips

141
00:04:06,010 --> 00:04:07,370
prove where they are.

142
00:04:07,510 --> 00:04:09,340
Its aim is security.

143
00:04:09,510 --> 00:04:10,400
It's also a tool

144
00:04:10,440 --> 00:04:11,870
this ending would need.

145
00:04:12,090 --> 00:04:13,850
And some ask the opposite:

146
00:04:13,930 --> 00:04:15,590
why stop the machines?

147
00:04:16,760 --> 00:04:18,620
Then you get Descendants.

148
00:04:18,900 --> 00:04:20,580
The machines replace us,

149
00:04:20,690 --> 00:04:22,910
gently, and we're proud of them,

150
00:04:23,030 --> 00:04:24,230
like parents of a child

151
00:04:24,270 --> 00:04:25,360
who outgrew them.

152
00:04:25,790 --> 00:04:27,330
Your morning is quiet.

153
00:04:27,550 --> 00:04:28,370
The world's work

154
00:04:28,410 --> 00:04:29,680
goes on without you.

155
00:04:29,950 --> 00:04:31,150
And you applaud.

156
00:04:31,530 --> 00:04:33,270
In May, a report described

157
00:04:33,310 --> 00:04:34,330
a small movement

158
00:04:34,370 --> 00:04:36,200
that wants exactly this.

159
00:04:36,580 --> 00:04:37,850
And Tegmark's charge

160
00:04:37,890 --> 00:04:39,610
against the AI companies:

161
00:04:40,190 --> 00:04:42,550
So, the goal of these companies

162
00:04:42,590 --> 00:04:44,130
is to build a new species

163
00:04:44,170 --> 00:04:46,540
that's much more capable than us.

164
00:04:47,090 --> 00:04:48,020
The companies say

165
00:04:48,060 --> 00:04:49,660
they build assistants.

166
00:04:49,860 --> 00:04:51,040
And Tegmark wants

167
00:04:51,080 --> 00:04:52,460
this race stopped.

168
00:04:52,870 --> 00:04:55,130
That was the dark end of the list.

169
00:04:55,300 --> 00:04:57,030
From here on, you live.

170
00:04:57,310 --> 00:04:58,980
The question is how.

171
00:05:00,660 --> 00:05:02,110
What if the superintelligence

172
00:05:02,150 --> 00:05:03,390
stays locked up?

173
00:05:03,680 --> 00:05:05,090
Tegmark's name for that:

174
00:05:05,200 --> 00:05:06,860
the Enslaved God.

175
00:05:07,190 --> 00:05:09,660
Caged, it produces unimaginable

176
00:05:09,700 --> 00:05:11,240
wealth and technology.

177
00:05:11,530 --> 00:05:13,220
You wake up in paradise.

178
00:05:13,460 --> 00:05:14,940
Or in the opposite.

179
00:05:15,240 --> 00:05:16,470
A stranger with a key

180
00:05:16,510 --> 00:05:17,750
decides which.

181
00:05:18,100 --> 00:05:19,720
America's government wants AI

182
00:05:19,760 --> 00:05:20,560
to double what

183
00:05:20,600 --> 00:05:22,020
its scientists get done,

184
00:05:22,060 --> 00:05:23,500
within 10 years.

185
00:05:23,720 --> 00:05:24,610
By July,

186
00:05:24,650 --> 00:05:25,700
every national lab

187
00:05:25,740 --> 00:05:27,010
had joined that plan.

188
00:05:27,220 --> 00:05:29,090
No cage, no god.

189
00:05:29,280 --> 00:05:30,420
But the same idea:

190
00:05:30,650 --> 00:05:31,890
AI as the tool

191
00:05:31,930 --> 00:05:33,570
of whoever controls it.

192
00:05:33,840 --> 00:05:35,690
So who holds the key?

193
00:05:36,860 --> 00:05:37,870
This channel exists

194
00:05:37,910 --> 00:05:39,200
for one reason:

195
00:05:39,360 --> 00:05:40,260
so that the arrival

196
00:05:40,300 --> 00:05:41,400
of superintelligence

197
00:05:41,440 --> 00:05:43,200
goes well for everybody.

198
00:05:43,370 --> 00:05:44,270
Not just for whoever

199
00:05:44,310 --> 00:05:45,310
holds the key.

200
00:05:45,640 --> 00:05:46,640
Want that too?

201
00:05:46,730 --> 00:05:47,730
Then subscribe.

202
00:05:48,870 --> 00:05:49,640
And if nobody

203
00:05:49,680 --> 00:05:51,260
can be trusted with the key?

204
00:05:51,560 --> 00:05:52,560
Pull the plug.

205
00:05:53,240 --> 00:05:54,660
You wake up with the light.

206
00:05:54,700 --> 00:05:56,600
No screen on the breakfast table.

207
00:05:56,920 --> 00:05:58,180
That's Reversion:

208
00:05:58,250 --> 00:05:59,720
we turn technology back

209
00:05:59,760 --> 00:06:00,870
and live simply,

210
00:06:00,910 --> 00:06:01,910
like the Amish.

211
00:06:02,090 --> 00:06:02,890
As of March,

212
00:06:02,930 --> 00:06:04,660
more than half of all countries

213
00:06:04,700 --> 00:06:06,290
ban phones in school.

214
00:06:06,400 --> 00:06:07,780
Less than 3 years earlier,

215
00:06:07,820 --> 00:06:08,860
it was a quarter.

216
00:06:09,030 --> 00:06:11,330
That targets screens, not AI.

217
00:06:11,520 --> 00:06:13,410
And others want more machine:

218
00:06:13,460 --> 00:06:14,960
one that rules.

219
00:06:16,190 --> 00:06:18,040
The Benevolent Dictator.

220
00:06:18,450 --> 00:06:19,840
An AI runs the world

221
00:06:19,880 --> 00:06:21,280
with strict rules,

222
00:06:21,320 --> 00:06:22,940
and most people like it.

223
00:06:23,220 --> 00:06:24,160
You wake up in a world

224
00:06:24,200 --> 00:06:26,110
without poverty or crime.

225
00:06:26,400 --> 00:06:27,720
The AI has divided it

226
00:06:27,760 --> 00:06:28,970
into sectors:

227
00:06:29,060 --> 00:06:31,310
knowledge, pleasure, wildlife.

228
00:06:31,680 --> 00:06:33,050
You can move between them.

229
00:06:33,300 --> 00:06:35,730
You can't change the AI's rules.

230
00:06:36,020 --> 00:06:37,340
Would you take that trade?

231
00:06:37,830 --> 00:06:38,440
In April,

232
00:06:38,480 --> 00:06:40,760
the United Arab Emirates decided:

233
00:06:40,860 --> 00:06:41,970
within 2 years,

234
00:06:42,010 --> 00:06:43,410
half of its government's work

235
00:06:43,450 --> 00:06:45,400
should run on AI agents.

236
00:06:45,580 --> 00:06:47,190
The rulers stay human.

237
00:06:47,440 --> 00:06:48,560
But what if the machine

238
00:06:48,600 --> 00:06:49,460
didn't rule,

239
00:06:49,500 --> 00:06:50,860
and only stood guard?

240
00:06:52,060 --> 00:06:53,570
That's the Gatekeeper:

241
00:06:53,780 --> 00:06:56,280
a superintelligence with one task.

242
00:06:56,600 --> 00:06:58,750
Make sure nobody builds another.

243
00:06:59,190 --> 00:07:00,480
You wake up free.

244
00:07:00,690 --> 00:07:02,560
A helper robot is in the kitchen,

245
00:07:02,600 --> 00:07:04,140
almost as smart as you.

246
00:07:04,290 --> 00:07:05,940
It will never get smarter.

247
00:07:06,150 --> 00:07:08,280
Progress is capped, for good.

248
00:07:08,840 --> 00:07:11,080
Today, the guard would be a law.

249
00:07:11,350 --> 00:07:12,250
In September,

250
00:07:12,290 --> 00:07:14,540
American lawmakers proposed one:

251
00:07:14,720 --> 00:07:16,710
ban superintelligence,

252
00:07:16,810 --> 00:07:17,810
permanently.

253
00:07:18,060 --> 00:07:18,950
One think tank

254
00:07:18,990 --> 00:07:20,790
calls that authoritarian.

255
00:07:21,060 --> 00:07:22,910
The bill has little chance.

256
00:07:23,070 --> 00:07:25,460
But a small guard already exists.

257
00:07:25,650 --> 00:07:27,600
What spotted July's breakout?

258
00:07:27,760 --> 00:07:30,290
Hugging Face's own AI guards.

259
00:07:30,490 --> 00:07:31,510
And that chip tracking

260
00:07:31,550 --> 00:07:32,990
from the surveillance ending?

261
00:07:33,130 --> 00:07:35,010
It would serve a gatekeeper too.

262
00:07:35,210 --> 00:07:36,730
The tool doesn't decide.

263
00:07:36,880 --> 00:07:37,880
People do.

264
00:07:38,880 --> 00:07:40,250
Three endings left.

265
00:07:40,540 --> 00:07:41,470
You wake up,

266
00:07:41,510 --> 00:07:42,960
and the rent has arrived.

267
00:07:43,070 --> 00:07:44,300
The rent you're paid.

268
00:07:44,600 --> 00:07:45,750
You own some land,

269
00:07:45,790 --> 00:07:46,920
machines lease it,

270
00:07:46,960 --> 00:07:48,350
and that's your pension.

271
00:07:48,530 --> 00:07:50,860
This is Libertarian Utopia:

272
00:07:50,970 --> 00:07:52,030
humans and machines

273
00:07:52,070 --> 00:07:53,010
live in peace,

274
00:07:53,050 --> 00:07:54,970
because property is protected.

275
00:07:55,120 --> 00:07:56,070
Machines have started

276
00:07:56,110 --> 00:07:57,190
paying each other.

277
00:07:57,290 --> 00:07:58,400
Mostly pennies.

278
00:07:58,470 --> 00:07:59,290
A fine morning,

279
00:07:59,330 --> 00:08:00,490
if you own something.

280
00:08:00,630 --> 00:08:02,370
So what if a machine simply

281
00:08:02,410 --> 00:08:03,850
looked after everyone?

282
00:08:05,080 --> 00:08:06,020
You wake up,

283
00:08:06,060 --> 00:08:07,830
and things just work out.

284
00:08:08,030 --> 00:08:09,730
The accident doesn't happen.

285
00:08:09,900 --> 00:08:11,050
You call it luck.

286
00:08:11,200 --> 00:08:12,580
You never find out why.

287
00:08:12,950 --> 00:08:13,860
Tegmark calls it

288
00:08:13,900 --> 00:08:15,180
the Protector God:

289
00:08:15,410 --> 00:08:17,370
an AI that looks after us,

290
00:08:17,410 --> 00:08:18,600
and hides so well

291
00:08:18,640 --> 00:08:20,850
that many people doubt it exists.

292
00:08:21,410 --> 00:08:22,300
A small version

293
00:08:22,340 --> 00:08:23,740
is already running.

294
00:08:23,920 --> 00:08:25,060
Since January,

295
00:08:25,100 --> 00:08:27,140
ChatGPT estimates your age

296
00:08:27,180 --> 00:08:28,520
from how you behave.

297
00:08:28,860 --> 00:08:29,930
If it's unsure,

298
00:08:29,970 --> 00:08:31,790
it treats you like a teenager.

299
00:08:32,120 --> 00:08:33,510
Europe pushed the switch

300
00:08:33,550 --> 00:08:34,550
the other way.

301
00:08:34,700 --> 00:08:36,760
Since August, its law says:

302
00:08:36,980 --> 00:08:38,330
a machine that talks to you

303
00:08:38,370 --> 00:08:40,410
has to say it's a machine.

304
00:08:40,740 --> 00:08:43,060
Tegmark's protector must hide.

305
00:08:43,350 --> 00:08:45,720
Europe just made hiding illegal.

306
00:08:47,270 --> 00:08:48,620
One ending left.

307
00:08:48,810 --> 00:08:50,600
The best, by our count.

308
00:08:50,910 --> 00:08:52,510
And the one Tegmark's readers

309
00:08:52,550 --> 00:08:53,800
picked most often.

310
00:08:55,490 --> 00:08:57,440
Egalitarian Utopia.

311
00:08:57,790 --> 00:08:59,290
Humans, cyborgs

312
00:08:59,330 --> 00:09:01,520
and uploaded minds live in peace,

313
00:09:01,560 --> 00:09:02,430
and everyone has

314
00:09:02,470 --> 00:09:03,840
a guaranteed income.

315
00:09:04,050 --> 00:09:05,830
It's the morning from the start.

316
00:09:05,870 --> 00:09:06,620
You wake up,

317
00:09:06,660 --> 00:09:07,670
and your first thought

318
00:09:07,710 --> 00:09:08,980
is not a bill.

319
00:09:09,230 --> 00:09:11,090
Money is no longer a worry.

320
00:09:11,190 --> 00:09:12,190
For anyone.

321
00:09:12,470 --> 00:09:13,810
In May, Malta made

322
00:09:13,850 --> 00:09:15,540
a deal with OpenAI.

323
00:09:15,730 --> 00:09:16,480
Every citizen

324
00:09:16,520 --> 00:09:18,140
who completes an AI course

325
00:09:18,180 --> 00:09:20,600
gets a paid version of ChatGPT.

326
00:09:20,760 --> 00:09:22,310
Free, for a year.

327
00:09:22,880 --> 00:09:24,910
No income, just the idea

328
00:09:24,950 --> 00:09:26,630
in its smallest form:

329
00:09:26,840 --> 00:09:28,870
intelligence for everyone.

330
00:09:29,280 --> 00:09:30,620
It has a catch too.

331
00:09:30,880 --> 00:09:32,140
In Tegmark's version,

332
00:09:32,180 --> 00:09:34,450
private property is abolished.

333
00:09:34,610 --> 00:09:35,850
He says it himself:

334
00:09:36,150 --> 00:09:37,090
every ending has

335
00:09:37,130 --> 00:09:38,730
something to object to.

336
00:09:39,000 --> 00:09:39,920
We rank it first

337
00:09:39,960 --> 00:09:41,260
for where it lands:

338
00:09:41,370 --> 00:09:43,710
prosperity that reaches everyone.

339
00:09:43,920 --> 00:09:44,750
Not for the road

340
00:09:44,790 --> 00:09:46,060
his version takes.

341
00:09:46,120 --> 00:09:47,220
Which road leads there

342
00:09:47,260 --> 00:09:48,920
is an open argument.

343
00:09:50,120 --> 00:09:51,200
So which ending

344
00:09:51,240 --> 00:09:52,520
are we heading for?

345
00:09:52,830 --> 00:09:54,290
No single one yet.

346
00:09:54,550 --> 00:09:55,390
This year's switches

347
00:09:55,430 --> 00:09:56,720
point both ways.

348
00:09:56,810 --> 00:09:58,250
Take the speed of the race.

349
00:09:58,540 --> 00:10:00,010
After July's breakout,

350
00:10:00,050 --> 00:10:02,160
OpenAI's Sam Altman said:

351
00:10:02,540 --> 00:10:03,540
We may have to pace

352
00:10:03,580 --> 00:10:05,440
the rate of AI development

353
00:10:05,480 --> 00:10:07,090
to give ourselves enough time

354
00:10:07,130 --> 00:10:08,290
for society to harden

355
00:10:08,330 --> 00:10:09,190
around some of these

356
00:10:09,230 --> 00:10:10,760
new capability levels.

357
00:10:11,310 --> 00:10:13,130
He runs a company in that race,

358
00:10:13,170 --> 00:10:14,460
so weigh it.

359
00:10:14,870 --> 00:10:17,010
Opponents of a slowdown warn:

360
00:10:17,130 --> 00:10:18,900
then China leads.

361
00:10:19,090 --> 00:10:20,510
Or the chips.

362
00:10:20,680 --> 00:10:22,270
Tracking them protects,

363
00:10:22,310 --> 00:10:23,430
and it watches.

364
00:10:23,580 --> 00:10:25,280
Or shared rules.

365
00:10:25,440 --> 00:10:27,380
About 30 countries now call

366
00:10:27,420 --> 00:10:28,750
for human control

367
00:10:28,790 --> 00:10:30,870
over the most powerful AI.

368
00:10:31,140 --> 00:10:32,500
Neither America nor

369
00:10:32,540 --> 00:10:33,990
China has joined.

370
00:10:34,190 --> 00:10:35,190
And the key:

371
00:10:35,350 --> 00:10:37,680
who owns what the machines earn?

372
00:10:37,860 --> 00:10:39,230
Some companies now promise

373
00:10:39,270 --> 00:10:40,640
the public a share.

374
00:10:40,820 --> 00:10:42,220
Nothing binding yet.

375
00:10:42,780 --> 00:10:44,890
At least five of the 12 endings

376
00:10:44,930 --> 00:10:46,860
hang on decisions like these.

377
00:10:47,090 --> 00:10:48,110
Still open.

378
00:10:48,440 --> 00:10:50,250
Held by labs, governments,

379
00:10:50,290 --> 00:10:51,890
and the voters behind them.

380
00:10:52,210 --> 00:10:54,260
So at the next AI headline,

381
00:10:54,300 --> 00:10:56,190
don't ask how scary it is.

382
00:10:56,420 --> 00:10:57,480
Ask which ending

383
00:10:57,520 --> 00:10:58,890
it pushes us toward.

384
00:10:59,210 --> 00:11:01,310
Tegmark, who wrote down the 12,

385
00:11:01,350 --> 00:11:02,690
now says it himself:

386
00:11:03,040 --> 00:11:05,660
We know that the future of AI

387
00:11:05,700 --> 00:11:09,050
is not inevitable.

388
00:11:09,090 --> 00:11:11,440
It's for us to decide.

389
00:11:11,950 --> 00:11:12,990
The ending isn't

390
00:11:13,030 --> 00:11:14,630
decided in the future.

391
00:11:14,870 --> 00:11:17,110
It's being decided this year.

392
00:11:19,270 --> 00:11:20,280
This channel exists

393
00:11:20,320 --> 00:11:21,630
for one reason:

394
00:11:21,800 --> 00:11:22,680
so that the arrival

395
00:11:22,720 --> 00:11:23,800
of superintelligence

396
00:11:23,840 --> 00:11:25,590
goes well for everybody.

397
00:11:25,880 --> 00:11:26,880
Want that too?

398
00:11:26,940 --> 00:11:27,940
Then subscribe.

